<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Sam'al</h1><p class="st-meta">920 BCE – 680 BCE (approx.) · capital Sam'al</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Sam'al, a small Aramaean-Luwian kingdom at Zincirli whose kings left some of the most vivid inscriptions of the Iron Age.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Sam'al arose in the 10th century BCE in a valley east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-mountains">Amanus</a> mountains, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islahiye">Islahiye</a>. According to its own inscriptions, a ruler named Gabbar founded the dynasty, and the land was also called Ya'diya. Its capital at Zincirli was a circular walled city.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilamuwa">Kilamuwa's</a> inscription boasts that he hired the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> against his enemies and improved the lot of his poor subjects. Later kings wrote in a local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a> dialect; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bar-rakib">Bar-Rakib</a> built palaces as a loyal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of Tiglath-Pileser III. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuttamuwa-stele">Kuttamuwa stele</a>, found in 2008, shows a belief in a soul dwelling in the stone.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Sam'al became an Assyrian province by c. 680 BCE; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esarhaddon">Esarhaddon</a> set up a victory stele in the city in 671 BCE. German excavations from 1888 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-chicago">University of Chicago</a> excavations from 2006 uncovered its gates and palaces.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/samal.jpg" alt="Sam'al" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Klaus-Peter Simon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zincirli1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>920 BCE – 680 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sam'al</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kilamuwa, Panamuwa II, Bar-Rakib</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Aramaean religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aramaic, Phoenician</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ya'diya, Zincirli</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-800&amp;focus=samal" aria-label="Sam'al on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5599 841 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sam'al lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5919 1097L6092 1134"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6092 1134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5919 1097h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5919 1097h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-800&amp;focus=samal">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

